ion":{"commit_sha":"516bca63e5ac540acb3eb862624d8082abd04301","position":"1786498681375687001-bc350c76-a837-485f-ba4d-ac76af67fd1e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c688376e21e6b38451b5f9e24ef13cfcd2eb82e102f302b9d2e2f9d7649ac36d","event_uuid":"5e95087a-3632-4995-ab4b-f3e4ac4b1396","position":{"commit_sha":"516bca63e5ac540acb3eb862624d8082abd04301","position":"1786498682158785001-5e95087a-3632-4995-ab4b-f3e4ac4b1396"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"316705f6ce782f79a54177a91c265c4b8d18af6f23c8e7bc72259cea9b79d010","event_uuid":"19dc528a-2d6b-42bd-8d7d-db6ae23af6ed","position":{"commit_sha":"c13a300b039114837eefcc3e28d7268ebdb5dcf7","position":"1786501479637742001-19dc528a-2d6b-42bd-8d7d-db6ae23af6ed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4df689f1539a96aebc21cc4f6798811bcebf9d0834e4dc0a3883ed1bec3e06b8","event_uuid":"96c3d944-0c56-47d6-ab05-b2385d721803","position":{"commit_sha":"7493e5ff7d3aa4fe852e0ab293ce6d169a813bfa","position":"1786501850819210614-96c3d944-0c56-47d6-ab05-b2385d721803"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f05fcf79fbcbdad11835cb31cdac399b432b1223f0397208a4de7d075a42a527","event_uuid":"e22f4060-028c-463c-9814-0a06cdcc5fdb","position":{"commit_sha":"d9d2ec8958df146ef50edb37d29ad6aa5d4519fa","position":"1786502202408592128-e22f4060-028c-463c-9814-0a06cdcc5fdb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC5 evidence (guard proven RED before the fix), recorded per the AC.\n\nRemoving the `sys.path` insert from `scripts/canary_bridge.py` and running the new guard:\n\n    scripts/canary_bridge.py:27: import alert_dedup (sys.path.insert above: False; derives from __file__: False)\n    AssertionError: a standalone bare `pytest` run of test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py failed:\n    1 failed, 1 passed  ->  after restoring the insert: 2 passed\n\nBoth guard tests go RED against the defect and GREEN with the fix.\n\nNote on the dynamic guard: the first draft used `--collect-only`, which stayed GREEN against the live defect — the failure surfaces at module-scoped fixture setup (where canary_bridge.py is loaded by path), which collection never reaches. The test now RUNS the module instead. Worth recording because it is the same change-detector trap this ticket is about.\n\nGates: lint + format + typecheck clean; full `tests/unit tests/scripts` = 10069 passed, 38 skipped, exit 0. Gerrit change 1606.","timestamp":1786501479637742001}],"created_at":1786122868627208001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4c9df924-92ef-4fd2-8aa1-f524a1f770f4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"63e8-9235-220f-4201"},{"link_uuid":"96c3d944-0c56-47d6-ab05-b2385d721803","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2c71-e399-301e-454c"},{"link_uuid":"e22f4060-028c-463c-9814-0a06cdcc5fdb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2053-8159-717e-4277"}],"description":"## Report\n\n`scripts/canary_bridge.py:26` does a bare `import alert_dedup`. That only resolves when\n`scripts/` is already on `sys.path`. Running the affected test file on its own fails:\n\n```\n$ python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py -q\nERROR ...::test_every_bug_close_carries_valid_class[heartbeat-alert-_heartbeat_recovery_env]\n  - ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'alert_dedup'\nERROR ...::test_every_bug_close_carries_valid_class[binding-drift-alert-_drift_recovery_env]\n  - ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'alert_dedup'\n1 passed, 2 errors\n```\n\nReproduced on `origin/main` with the repo venv on PATH.\n\n## Provenance — introduced today, not pre-existing\n\n`scripts/alert_dedup.py` was ADDED by `0767c38ebb` (ticket 63e8, \"route dependency\nadvisories by lane\"). That change correctly EXTRACTED the dedup helpers out of\n`canary_bridge.py` rather than duplicating them — the extraction was the right call — but it\nleft the consumers importing the new module by bare name.\n\n## Why it matters even though CI is green\n\nCI's full run passes because `tests/scripts/conftest.py:32-38` inserts repo-root `scripts/`\non `sys.path` at collection time, and that process-wide side effect leaks into every\nlater-collected module in the same session — including `tests/unit/`, which has no such\ninsert of its own. The failure only appears when the file is run as a SUBSET — which is what\ndevelopers and agents do constantly while iterating. A test that passes in CI and fails when\nyou run it directly trains people to distrust the suite.\n\n## Chosen mechanism (AC2 decision, stated up front)\n\n**An explicit `sys.path` insert of the script's own directory, immediately above the sibling\nimport** — the pattern already established in this repo by\n`scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:46-51`. Rationale, and why the two alternatives are\nrejected:\n\n- *Package-relative import* — rejected. These modules are executed as standalone scripts by\n  workflow YAML (`python scripts/canary_bridge.py heartbeat-alert …`,\n  `scripts/dependency_audit.py gate`). A relative import raises\n  `ImportError: attempted relative import with no known parent package` under that\n  invocation, so it would trade a test-only failure for a production-canary failure.\n- *Making `scripts/` a real package* — rejected. Adding `scripts/__init__.py` changes how\n  every script in the directory is resolved by every existing caller (workflows, Makefile,\n  pre-commit), which is a far larger blast radius than the defect, and is not\n  behavior-preserving.\n\nThe chosen insert is invocation-independent: it derives the directory from `__file__`, so it\nholds under `python scripts/x.py`, `python -m pytest`, bare `pytest`, and\n`importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` alike. It is idempotent (guarded by a membership\ncheck) and does not reorder any path entry that is already present.\n\n## Sweep of sibling call sites (AC3)\n\nEvery bare import under `scripts/` of a module that lives in `scripts/` or `tests/`:\n\n| Site | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `scripts/canary_bridge.py:26` `import alert_dedup` | **UNGUARDED — fix here** |\n| `scripts/dependency_audit.py:50` `import alert_dedup` | **UNGUARDED — fix here** |\n| `scripts/calibrate_completion_floor.py:24` `from gold_set_completion import …` | SAFE — line 22 explicitly inserts `tests/unit` derived from `__file__` immediately above it |\n| `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:51` `import jira_dc_field_readiness` | SAFE — lines 46-48 insert `scripts/` from `__file__`; this is the precedent pattern |\n| `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:59` `from _engine_path import engine_dir` | SAFE — lines 57-58 insert `tests/` from `__file__` |\n\nThe sweep is valid as of the sha it runs against and is re-run against merged `main` before\npush.\n\n## Guard (AC4/AC5) — closing the other half of the class\n\nTicket `a371` (merged `1db88c92d7`) landed `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py`, which\nAST-scans for `tests.`-rooted imports **under `tests/`**. It does not look at `scripts/`, so\nthe class is only half-guarded. This adds the companion:\n`tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py`, same AST-scan shape, asserting that every\nbare import under `scripts/` naming a module that is only resolvable via a directory insert\nis preceded by that insert in the same file — plus a subprocess check that the affected test\nmodule collects when run alone.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1 — the reported repro passes standalone.**\n  Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py -q` exits 0 with\n  0 errors (repo venv on PATH, no wrapper).\n- [ ] **AC2 — the import is resolved by an explicit, invocation-independent mechanism.** Both\n  fixed sites derive the directory from `__file__` and insert it idempotently above the\n  import; neither relies on ambient `sys.path` ordering.\n  Verify (asserts the insert itself, not merely the token `__file__`):\n  `python -c \"import sys; bad=[p for p in ['scripts/canary_bridge.py','scripts/dependency_audit.py'] for w in [open(p).read().split('import alert_dedup')[0]] if not ('sys.path.insert' in w and '__file__' in w)]; print(bad); sys.exit(1 if bad else 0)\"`\n  exits 0 and prints `[]`.\n- [ ] **AC3 — sibling call sites swept and classified.** The table above enumerates all five\n  bare sibling-import sites and states which are safe and why.\n  Verify (AST scan that distinguishes sibling imports from stdlib/third-party by resolving\n  each imported top-level name against a real file under `scripts/` or `tests/**`, then\n  compares the resulting set to the five documented rows — exits 0 and prints `OK` only on\n  an exact match):\n  `python -c \"$(cat <<'PY'\nimport ast, pathlib, sys\nroot = pathlib.Path('.')\nsib = {p.stem for p in root.glob('scripts/*.py')} | {p.stem for p in root.glob('tests/**/*.py')}\nfound = set()\nfor p in sorted(root.glob('scripts/*.py')):\n    tree = ast.parse(p.read_text(), filename=str(p))\n    for n in ast.walk(tree):\n        names = [a.name for a in n.names] if isinstance(n, ast.Import) else (\n            [n.module] if isinstance(n, ast.ImportFrom) and n.level == 0 and n.module else [])\n        for m in names:\n            if m.split('.')[0] in sib and m.split('.')[0] != p.stem:\n                found.add(f\"{p}:{n.lineno}:{m}\")\nexpected = {\n 'scripts/canary_bridge.py:__L__:alert_dedup',\n 'scripts/dependency_audit.py:__L__:alert_dedup',\n 'scripts/calibrate_completion_floor.py:__L__:gold_set_completion',\n 'scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:__L__:jira_dc_field_readiness',\n 'scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:__L__:_engine_path'}\nnorm = {':'.join([a, '__L__', c]) for a, _, c in (f.split(':') for f in found)}\nprint(sorted(norm - expected) or 'OK'); sys.exit(1 if norm - expected else 0)\nPY\n)\"`\n  (line numbers are normalized out so the check survives the insert shifting them).\n- [ ] **AC4 — the a371 guard has a companion covering `scripts/`.**\n  Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py -q` exits 0, and the\n  new file exists.\n- [ ] **AC5 — the guard is proven RED against the defect.**\n  Verify: reverting the `sys.path` insert in `scripts/canary_bridge.py` and re-running\n  `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py -q` FAILS naming\n  `scripts/canary_bridge.py`; restoring it makes it pass. Run this before landing and record\n  the output in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] **AC6 — no behavior change and no regression.**\n  Verify: `make lint && make typecheck && python -m pytest tests/unit tests/scripts -q`\n  all pass.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nAny change to what `canary_bridge.py` or `dependency_audit.py` DO — this is an import-\nresolution repair only. No CLI surface, no argv, no output text changes.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/canary_bridge.py","reason":"add idempotent __file__-derived sys.path insert of scripts/ above the bare `import alert_dedup`"},{"path":"scripts/dependency_audit.py","reason":"same unguarded bare `import alert_dedup`; same insert"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py","reason":"NEW companion guard to a371: AST-scan scripts/ for bare sibling imports lacking a path insert, plus standalone-collection subprocess check"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2053-8159-717e-4277"],["relates_to","2c71-e399-301e-454c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bc350c76-a837-485f-ba4d-ac76af67fd1e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"291e-7b48-3f24-41c6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"canary_bridge's bare 'import alert_dedup' resolves only when scripts/ is on sys.path; subset test runs error","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["62302265-6941-4fbe-9371-4330f1726943","4c9df924-92ef-4fd2-8aa1-f524a1f770f4","9ee25a9d-8fcb-4053-b5f1-8fbea15deb79","caa8f58f-6298-4248-9bd3-e3b17c7653d9","f9d9f2f9-742a-4c50-ae60-bf5c3db901b1","586936ad-7bb4-49aa-a060-0552cf96b9db","f32fe2d5-9919-46a8-a092-a31a051e1131","bc350c76-a837-485f-ba4d-ac76af67fd1e","5e95087a-3632-4995-ab4b-f3e4ac4b1396","19dc528a-2d6b-42bd-8d7d-db6ae23af6ed","96c3d944-0c56-47d6-ab05-b2385d721803","e22f4060-028c-463c-9814-0a06cdcc5fdb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786502202408592129,"uuid":"59e63fbf-f4cc-4234-99cc-2a2d0977c134"}